🚨 PART 1: Things NOT Right for the MVP (Bugs & Issues)

🔴 Critical Bugs

1. Hardcoded dev store password in memory (rawPassword)
institutes.service.ts stores rawPassword: adminPassword on the in-memory user objects. auth.service.ts fallbackLogin checks memUser.rawPassword (plaintext) against memUser.password (bcrypt). If the DB is down, any user with a bcrypt-hashed password can't login because rawPassword is only set during that session's creation — on server restart, loadDevStore() loads users with bcrypt password but NO rawPassword, making all offline/restored users unable to login.

- Files: backend/src/auth/auth.service.ts:112, backend/src/institutes/institutes.service.ts:133, backend/src/users/users.service.ts:68

2. Duplicate records from dev store + DB merge
Every "findAll" method returns [...dbRecords, ...memoryMatches] — when both DB and dev store have the same records (e.g., after DB comes back online), users see duplicates on every list.

- Files: Every service — institutes.service.ts:199, courses.service.ts:133, lessons.service.ts:116, enrollments.service.ts:134, etc.

3. syncStore() doesn't pass ALL keys, silently dropping data
Each module's syncStore() function only passes a subset of keys. For example, courses.service.ts:17 does:
saveDevStore({ institutes: MEMORY_INSTITUTES, users: MEMORY_USERS, courses: MEMORY_COURSES });
This drops enrollments, lessons, attendance, tests, announcements, live classes, video progress every time a course is created. Same pattern in every module — overwriting the dev store with a partial snapshot.

4. Super Admin can't access institutes via API when DB fails
findAll() in institutes service throws if DB fails AND the memory array is empty — no graceful fallback to a seeded default.

5. Attendance model uses DateTime for date field, unique constraint breaks
The @@unique([courseId, studentId, date]) on Attendance uses full DateTime. If a teacher marks attendance for the same student on the same day but at a slightly different time (2026-07-28T10:00:00Z vs 2026-07-28T11:00:00Z), the upsert creates a duplicate rather than updating.

🟠 Security Issues

6. Plaintext passwords in localStorage
User object stored in localStorage includes sensitive fields. While password isn't there, the Institute object is exposed with full details. No encryption on client storage.

7. No token expiry validation on frontend
auth.ts sets a cookie with max-age=86400 (24h) but the JWT token itself has no expiry configured anywhere in the JWT strategy. Tokens never expire.

- File: backend/src/auth/strategies/jwt.strategy.ts — likely missing expiresIn in JWT sign options

8. CORS origin is environment-dependent but no .env.example exists
main.ts reads process.env.FRONTEND_URL but there's no .env.example or .env documentation. If someone deploys without setting it, CORS falls back to localhost:3000 and breaks.

9. Super Admin password admin123 is hardcoded
In seed.ts AND in the dev store fallback. 1-click demo login on the login page exposes it directly. Anyone who accesses the login page can see all accounts.

10. Courses controller allows TEACHER to delete courses — no, wait, it doesn't ✅ CORRECT: DELETE is @Roles(UserRole.INSTITUTE_ADMIN) only. But PATCH allows TEACHER to update courses (including reassigning teachers), which they shouldn't be able to do.

11. Test questions expose correctAnswer to the frontend
In tests.service.ts:135, findByCourse selects correctAnswer: true in the question results. Students can inspect the API response to see the right answer before starting.

🟡 UX & Logic Issues

12. Student "Retake Test" button doesn't create a new attempt — it shows the old result
When a student clicks "Start Test" on a previously taken test, the modal opens. But submitting again simply creates a NEW attempt — the old lastAttempt is only used for display, not to prevent retakes. No retake limit or cooldown.

13. No enrollment count validation
The enroll student flow replaces ALL enrollments for a course (enrollments.service.ts:79-83 deletes then re-adds). If the API call fails mid-way, some students lose their enrollment. This is a destructive overwrite, not an additive operation.

14. Student attendance defaults to 100% with no data
When getStudentAttendance finds 0 records, it returns percentage: 100. A student with no attendance marks looks like perfect attendance. Should be 0 or N/A.

15. No loading/empty states on announcement banners
If announcements API fails, teacher and student dashboards silently catch the error. The dashboard shows no announcements but also no error — the user doesn't know if announcements failed to load or there genuinely are none.

16. Course creation assigns the first found teacher, not a valid one
courses.service.ts:45-49: if no teacherId is provided, it picks this.prisma.user.findFirst({ where: { instituteId } }) — this could be a STUDENT, not necessarily a teacher.

17. Live classes findByCourse doesn't filter past sessions
All live classes (past and future) are shown. A student sees "Upcoming Live Class Alerts" for sessions that happened last week.

🟣 Code Quality Issues

18. catch (e) {} silent swallows everywhere
Almost every catch block in the codebase has an empty body or only a this.logger.warn(). If the DB fails silently and the dev store also has an error, the user gets a 200 OK with no data and no indication anything went wrong.

19. loadDevStore and saveDevStore are synchronous but the file operations are async
dev-store.ts uses synchronous fs.readFileSync/fs.writeFileSync. This blocks the event loop on every API call.

20. No input sanitization on text fields
Description, title, content fields accept arbitrary HTML/script tags. Stored XSS is possible if content is rendered without escaping (e.g., in announcement banners).

21. Mix of thumbnail and thumbnailUrl field names
Schema has thumbnail (String?), but frontend checks course.thumbnailUrl || course.thumbnail. The DTO has both @IsOptional() thumbnailUrl? and @IsOptional() thumbnail?. This is inconsistent.

22. Page metadata says "Create Next App"
layout.tsx still has the default Next.js metadata: title: "Create Next App" and description: "Generated by create next app".

23. No TypeScript strict mode in any config
Both tsconfig.json files likely don't have strict: true — the heavy use of any types throughout confirms this.

24. Circular imports through dev-store
Each service imports from other services' MEMORY_* variables. lessons.service.ts imports from live-classes.service.ts, which imports from lessons.service.ts — this is a circular dependency chain that works only because of JavaScript's module caching.

