✨ PART 2: Features Worth Adding Early

👑 High Impact / Low Effort

1. Bulk CSV Student Import
Institute admins upload a CSV with student names/emails/passwords. Compose rows from the list, batch-create accounts. Could handle 50+ students in one go instead of one-by-one.

2. Forgot Password Flow (UI)
Backend DTOs exist but no frontend. Add a "Forgot Password?" link on login, a simple form that accepts email, and a "Check your inbox" message. Wire to SendGrid later.

3. Student Test History Page
Students can see all their past attempts, scores, and pass/fail across courses. Currently only the last attempt is shown per test.

4. Publish/Unpublish Toggle on Test
Tests auto-publish on creation. Give teachers a publish toggle so they can create tests in draft mode first.

5. Teacher Dashboard Analytics
Add simple stats: average test scores across students, attendance trends, most-watched lessons. All data is already in the DB — just need a summary API.

6. Video Lecture Duration Display
Show video duration on lesson cards. The duration field exists in the Lesson model, but it's never displayed on the frontend.

📱 Medium Impact / Medium Effort

7. Role-Specific Landing pages
When logged in, the root / redirects the user to their role dashboard. Currently it just shows the generic landing page.

8. Toast Notification System
Every success/error currently uses alert() (native browser dialog) or a temporary inline message. A toast system would be far less intrusive.

9. Course Categories / Tags
Let admins tag courses (e.g., "JEE", "NEET", "Class 11", "Physics") and let students filter by tags. Simple text field on Course, no new tables needed.

10. Student Dashboard Progress Summary
On the main student dashboard, show overall progress across ALL courses (e.g., "45% complete across 3 courses"), not just per-course.

11. Attendance Report Export
Download attendance sheet as CSV/PDF for a given course and date range. Useful for institutes to maintain physical records.

12. Edit Lesson Content
Teachers can't edit a lesson after uploading. They have to delete and re-create. Add an edit modal with pre-filled fields.

13. Teacher Profile Page
Show teacher's assigned courses, their students, and quick stats. Currently teachers are just a name in a table.

🏗️ MVP-Pipeline Blockers

14. File Upload Handler (S3/R2)
This is the biggest remaining MVP gap. Currently everything is URL-based. For real institutes, teachers need to upload videos and PDFs directly. Without this, you can't launch.

15. Payment Gateway Integration
Courses have a price field but no way to collect payments. Even if you defer this, you need at least a "Request Payment" flow or a note saying "Contact institute for payment."

16. Health Check Endpoint
Before deploying, add GET /api/v1/health that returns DB status, uptime, memory usage. Essential for monitoring.

17. Rate Limiting
No rate limiting on any endpoint. A malicious actor could hit /auth/login with brute-force attempts or spam the announcements API.

